 ## Key Design Decisions
 
 - **Commands over HTTPS, one authoritative board per event.** Editors submit commands to the server, which assigns each committed edit one event revision. Peer-to-peer or browser-side merging was rejected: the tenets require one authoritative revision regardless of delivery route, and offline editing is a non-goal.
+- **Committed changes over self-hosted WebSockets.** The service operates persistent browser connections and revision replay to provide fast updates without a realtime vendor dependency. Five-second HTTPS polling would reduce connection operations but add repeated reads and delivery lag; a hosted realtime service would reduce connection operations but add recurring fees and provider coupling. See [Realtime Change Delivery](decisions/realtime-change-delivery.md).
